+# Direct Source r38 → pseudocode r12 translation review
+
+## Objective and scope
+
+Finish the translation, not merely its entry manifest. When translation exposes a domain decision, decide it in Source first and translate that decision. Preserve Source hierarchy, inputs/results, branches, generation/consumption, mutation/failure atomicity, lifecycle and resource ownership. Activate the complete hierarchy and retire the old flat pseudocode. Modified files, the actual numeric patch and its explanation must be in one commit (user's latest instruction).
+
+Baseline: `57b4731f1ede5a75b22846652e12f556ed826bec`. Source r38 closure evidence is `review-20261017-001-source-r38-closure.md`; this review is NOT a substitute for that Source review. No application-code or optional verification-model translation is claimed here.
+
+## Prompt → artifact / completion checklist
+
+| Requirement | Concrete artifact / inspection |
+|---|---|
+| Return to Source rather than stopping at ambiguous domain meaning | Source r38 decisions/reasons/producer-consumer table in the Source closure review; actual eight changed Source files, including the common settings JSON |
+| Direct whole translation, same logical hierarchy | 15 active `.pcal` owner files, listed in the checker and Source-entry trace; old ten flat files deleted, root system replaced |
+| Every Source entry and original inputs | All 163 functions/methods across the fourteen nonempty Python owners, with owner-qualified duplicate names and original arity; zero-entry public `__init__` maps to the contract file. Actions generates per-entry Source and pseudocode paths/lines/signatures |
+| All public methods, not a generic replacement envelope | All 87 Source API keys; 60 explicit wrapper branches, remaining official queries/selections/adapter/exports; Source-specific success/failure/None/False/exception behavior retained |
+| Real branch/algorithm translation beyond a manifest | Per-owner semantic inspection below; candidate/read-context expansions, formats, calculations and cleanup are present in the active files, not external temporary drafts |
+| Single read/commit authority and failure preservation | Attempt/read parameters bind existing Source authority/candidate; final guard→validation→replacement is non-yielding; rejected commands do not reconcile or run success reads |
+| Actual source lineage/fingerprints and current status | `development-versions.json` r38/r12 and cumulative Actions version gate; unchanged application/model remain honestly stale |
+| Verification does not claim unsupported proof | Static checker + artifact scope explicit; no Source execution, application tests/build, PlusCal parser or TLC result is claimed |
+| Same-commit patch and modified files | Numeric patch is generated from the real staged semantic diff against baseline; pair is then staged with all modifications and committed atomically using Git, not sequential Contents writes |
+| No transient work product remains an alternate authority | Active hierarchy is authoritative; temporary `./.work/plan022/pseudocode` staging copies are removed after activation/verification, not published as parallel modules |
+
+## Actual semantic review, not just name coverage
+
+| Owner / corresponding `.pcal` | Compared Source semantics and inspected translation |
+|---|---|
+| `system` | Config/validated initial Project → Application query/FSM scalar input → renderer core startup → ready → API exposure/UI mounting. No system FSM or default CSV creation; root enters the declared initialization procedure. |
+| `backend/project_state` | Fixed roots/instance defaults from one config; visible/current identity resolution including ID/index zero; missing versus explicit null; all registered query kinds, detached scalar intents and postcommit reconciliation. Reconcile reset/swap/merge/move → resolve current refs → explicit graph hint → chart-scoped original-position map → retain valid prior index; unrelated CSV choice stays independent. Surface/export figures use the same captured Project, not selected CSV or a later registry read. |
+| `backend/project_efsm` | Every declared command branch has candidate calculation. Final authority freshness, revalidation and single commit; load/file waits recalculate. Asset create/replace/delete/trash/move/directory, graph add/edit/move/delete/palette/convert, image/connect/import, grid/merge/split/style, annotation/appearance/export settings. Actual changed IDs/paths/owners and reference maps derive from pre/post, never caller plans. Projection effect uses actual visible inputs/reference multiplicities. |
+| `backend/assets_files` | Canonical VFS segment and collision rules, stale replace rejection before available-path branch, ordered atomic batch candidate, copied original bytes, raw JSON/CSV/TSV parsing, explicit synthetic encoding, CRC/STORE/version/path checks. Typed XML preserves null/bool/zero/empty with strict unknown/nonfinite handling. FFPX splits/reassembles documents/slot geometry/settings/graphs and copied media; owned-byte loop resets its index. FFSX always has assets metadata, remaps only actual CSV refs, and installs one same-candidate chart with new actual IDs/paths. |
+| `backend/graphs` | All fifteen entries; same-candidate CSV resolution, no implicit live fallback. Existing valid x/y preserved, numeric body scan and sole-column fallback; paired row division→log/reciprocal→finite filtering; visible/type/style/extension precedence and axis placeholder product. Explicit axes/layout/default normalization and imported inverse mapping. Conversion builds the actual CSV model and bytes at a current unique path, removes linked conversion rows and rebuilds against that candidate; empty conversion does not invent data. |
+| `backend/layout_annotations` | Reference geometry/grid bounds and merge spans; current-label read copy; exact format/parentheses; exact-string contiguous caption runs, initial empties, gaps, label prefix, one-space separation and append-at-end. Pure candidate output, no Backend-to-Frontend event or config instance data. |
+| `application/adapter` | Validated scalar selection before FSM send; command success alone triggers reconciliation and render input. Exactly-once task callback; busy-before-work, returned rejection/cancel completes, thrown error publishes failure then ready and propagates original error. No alternate command registry or candidate builder. |
+| `application/public_api/contract` | 87 actual Source methods mapped; 11 import/export lifecycle bindings wrap once, nested helpers do not reenter. Reads are official current queries. Selected reads use copied current selection scalars. Wrapper arguments are Source call arguments, not a new public wire DTO. Six replaced lower public names do not remain as a legacy bridge. |
+| `application/public_api/assets` | Current file/collision/plan queries; Application chooser once, completed plans reserved locally, cancellation before mutation. Create-empty commits once then selects via validated event, no fabricated rollback. Single-file/FFSX/project routes, captured initial slot and ordered router with previous commits retained on later cancel/error. Directory batch remains one atomic candidate. Original bytes are downloaded; declared None/bool/path/copy return distinctions retained. |
+| `application/public_api/graphs` | Add routing, explicit identities/new edits, same-index move read-only success, delete null hint, header return from actual committed CSV, postcommit chart/settings reads only. Import/export go through declared Source lifecycle/public bindings; no independent current-CSV override on graph commit. |
+| `application/public_api/layout_annotations` | All 35 entries. Project/slot/image/asset selection, settings return rules, nested axes versus whole UI palette behavior; zoom/lock first positive reference width and reset/unlock semantics remain Frontend-local. Export queries supply one-shot inputs; renderer's saved/rejected outcome is forwarded unchanged. |
+| `frontend/interface_fsm` | All sixteen events and four methods; no Backend imports. Model-to-fsm nonnull same-slot selection clears graph index but retains valid independent asset; user/explicit deselection clears both. Validated-only reconcile, local zoom/busy/lifecycle transitions and ready recovery. |
+| `frontend/mantine_ui` | Five entries. Single chooser modal lifetime/cancel, one public lifecycle owner, supplied palette roles/shades/contrast, local layout interaction and one continuous drop route. No UI default/config/Project mirror. |
+| `frontend/renderer` | Twenty entries. Supplied figures only; current host/slot/chart/generation identity, stale completion disposal and task/surface-owned handles. Selection before action, content-interaction drop/click guard. Caption is measured/emitted once at reference width and the same lines are painted; target W/R scaling without another DPI multiplication; explicit height subtracts caption and rejects impossible cells before handoff. Both export paths finally release only owned resources and return explicit Source outcomes. |
+| `portable_build` | Existing source inputs → inline/split distribution, copy/verification order and output layout; platform file/encoding primitives remain below Source, no new build model. |
+
+## Challenges and rejected shortcuts
+
+- Entry/API counts alone are insufficient. The reviewed control/field/context/ownership paths above, including the Source corrections, are the semantic evidence; the automated trace only checks structural omissions/typos.
+- Undefined full constructors, document assemblers, mutation-effect calculations and single-file collision choice were expanded, not relabeled as platform primitives. Numeric record operations, native XML/ZIP/UTF-8/base64/DOM/codec mechanics remain legitimate lower primitives under the explicit Source contracts.
+- A public universal bool/envelope, persistent transaction token, duplicate Project read store, forced CSV reselection, and new generic command engine were rejected because they change Source meaning or authority.
+- This is language-neutral procedure composition, not a claim that cross-owner procedures form a standalone executable TLC module. The optional verification model remains a separately stale layer.
+
+## Verdict / execution record
+
+Semantic inspection supports complete direct translation of Source r38 and activation as pseudocode r12; no known remaining domain placeholder is intentionally deferred to implementation. This verdict covers translation, NOT application parity or formal proof. Required structural/cumulative Actions verification is pending at preparation time; actual run/commit/results must be appended after execution, without treating this review text or a complete manifest as a passing run.
